        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If the slab has to survive winter, salt and cars, choose penetrating chemistry and accept that the driveway will look exactly the same afterwards. That is the product doing its job, not failing to.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If the slab exists to be looked at — stamped, coloured, exposed aggregate, sheltered from the worst of the weather — choose an acrylic, add a slip additive, and plan on recoating every few years. The mistake is not picking one over the other; it is picking the decorative product for the structural job.
          </p>
        </div>

